! Placement step 4 — residency follows placement

The projector reads the selected bag's mirror, skips effect records by record kind, and retains only the TW5 temp/state plus temp-layer preference filters. The former daemon, VM, manifest, realm announcement, swarm, and nexus-handle title residency gates are removed. The kahua stage accepts control-shaped titles as ordinary content in its selected store. The disk ingress ward checks the vessel's mirror registry and requires the source path to fall under a mirror for the selected destination; control and secret homes refuse LOAD by name. Arbitrary-directory LOAD into ordinary working layers remains available through the existing LOAD gesture, followed by MOVE for promotion. Carry's in-memory import path still submits INGEST directly and has not yet been converted to that named road. The active daemon working-layer mirror is withheld while control writers still target that layer; this is an incomplete safety hold under the operator ruling, not a completed placement.

Red coverage: cross-mirror source rejection, private-home LOAD refusal, receipt-shaped title accepted in the selected ordinary bag, manifest-shaped title follows its selected mirror, realm announcements and WHO handles follow the crossroads mirror, and kahua accepts control-shaped content.

Validation status: see `PLACE-HANDBACK.md`; full package suites and final build/stamp/typecheck pass remain required.

Proposed commit subject: `lar:///ha.ka.ba/placement/lets-mirrors-decide-residency`

